# Copy to `.env` and fill in as needed. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# ── LLM API keys (only for examples/using-mcp-with-agents/) ──────────────────
# The mock server itself needs NO API keys. These are only read by the agent
# example scripts that drive an LLM against the mock.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Mock server settings (all optional; BACKLOT_-prefixed, see backlot/config.py) ───
# Sensible defaults are baked in; override only when you need to. Docker Compose passes whatever is
# set here into the container (the `env_file:` entry in docker-compose.yml), and `backlot serve` run
# directly reads this file too. The full table of settings and defaults is in docs/configuration.md.
#
# Org identity is normally derived from the corpus's dominant email domain.
# Set these to override the derivation entirely:
# BACKLOT_ORG_NAME=
# BACKLOT_ORG_DOMAIN=
#
# Auth: a caller presenting the admin token bypasses ACL filtering.
# BACKLOT_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# BACKLOT_EXPOSE_TOKENS=
#
# Paths (defaults resolve under the current working directory's data/ dir):
# BACKLOT_DATA_DIR=
#
# SQLite read tuning. The defaults suit the corpus most people serve; a deployment holding a much
# larger one raises all three — the mmap at or above the DB's own size so the first request after an
# idle period does not pay a cold-read penalty, and the busy timeout high enough that a read rides
# out an out-of-band FTS rebuild's commit instead of surfacing a 500:
# BACKLOT_SQLITE_MMAP_MB=
# BACKLOT_SQLITE_CACHE_MB=
# BACKLOT_SQLITE_BUSY_MS=
